{"id":"CVE-2015-9235","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2018-05-29T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T23:05:54.010Z","description":"In jsonwebtoken node module before 4.2.2 it is possible for an attacker to bypass verification when a token digitally signed with an asymmetric key (RS/ES family) of algorithms but instead the attacker send a token digitally signed with a symmetric algorithm (HS* family).","cwe":["CWE-20 Improper Input Validation (CWE-20)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"HackerOne","product":"jsonwebtoken node module","versions":["affected <4.2.2"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://nodesecurity.io/advisories/17","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/auth0/node-jsonwebtoken/commit/1bb584bc382295eeb7ee8c4452a673a77a68b687","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://auth0.com/blog/2015/03/31/critical-vulnerabilities-in-json-web-token-libraries/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.timmclean.net/2015/02/25/jwt-alg-none.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2015-9236","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2018-05-31T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T04:15:13.448Z","description":"Hapi versions less than 11.0.0 implement CORS incorrectly and allowed for configurations that at best returned inconsistent headers and at worst allowed cross-origin activities that were expected to be forbidden. If the connection has CORS enabled but one route has it off, and the route is not GET, the OPTIONS prefetch request will return the default CORS headers and then the actual request will go through and return no CORS headers. This defeats the purpose of turning CORS on the route.","cwe":["CWE-284 Improper Access Control - Generic (CWE-284)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"HackerOne","product":"hapi node module","versions":["affected <11.0.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/hapijs/hapi/issues/2850","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://github.com/hapijs/hapi/issues/2840","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://nodesecurity.io/advisories/45","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2015-9238","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"hackerone","published":"2018-05-31T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T17:43:37.504Z","description":"secure-compare 3.0.0 and below do not actually compare two strings properly. compare was actually comparing the first argument with itself, meaning the check passed for any two strings of the same length.","cwe":["CWE-697 Incorrect Comparison (CWE-697)"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"HackerOne","product":"secure-compare node module","versions":["affected <=3.0.0"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/vdemedes/secure-compare/pull/1","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://nodesecurity.io/advisories/50","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["nodejs"]}
